{"type":"thinking","text":"V1 is decent composition but window is a blank washed-out panel! Outside scene missing because likely later glass? Wait window pane content shows pale cream, no sky/hills. Why? We drew sky etc, then we drew `glass` overlays? Those are low alpha. Could be outer casing or pane frame filled over window. Let's inspect order:\n- Draw window view.\n- soft_poly_shadow around window (blurred shadow) - not fill interior? soft_poly_shadow with big window points, alpha 75, blur 12. It generates shadow filled polygon then blurs, would darken interior slightly but not obscure.\n- outer casing: `grad_rect(base, (218,72,1074,660))` fills entire rectangle including window! Then rr fills etc. Yes, we full-filled outer casing across whole window. Need draw frame as border, not filled rectangle. Should not fill interior. Same for several layers. Need composite ring shape rather than full fill.\n\nNeed fix window frame: define outer casing as ring: use mask with outer rounded rect minus inner rect. Our `grad_rect` fills all. Could draw solid fill using `rr` ring? We can draw outer frame in 4 bars or create ring mask. Simple: draw casing only in areas around pane:\n- Outer casing bars: top (218,72,1074,110), left (218,72,252,660), right (1040,72,1074,660), bottom (218,628,1074,660). But corner joins okay if bars overlap. Use fill/outline.\n- More manageable: remove current fills/overlays and redraw.\nAt present, window is blank due to full outer casing fill grad and then many rectangle fills, all covering. Need patch:\nReplace section:\n```\n# outer casing\ngrad_rect(...)\nrr...\n...\nrr pane frame...\nrr inner...\n```\nwith bars or use ring mask. Better create helper `frame_ring` that draws gradient via ring mask. Let's implement a local function in section:\n```\nframe = Image.new('RGBA',(CW,CH),(0,0,0,0))\n# mask = outer rounded rect fill white minus inner rounded rect\nmask=Image.new('L',...)\nmd.rounded_rectangle outer fill 255\nmd.rounded_rectangle inner