04,1040,628; inner 258,110,1034,622) dark outline.\n5. muntins.\n\nNeed not fill pane. Gradient ring local. Implement:\n```\ndef grad_ring(im,b_out,b_in,router,rinner,c1,c2,horizontal=False,outline=None,width=0):\n  bbox out; g=gradient_size; mask rounded outer filled; inner rounded zero; g.putalpha(mask); im.alpha_composite\n  optionally draw outlines clipping? \n```\nWe can draw outlines via redrawing ring? For outlines use `rr` only draws outline with no fill (good). Existing rr for trim ring no fill, okay.\nUse `grad_ring` for casing and maybe pane frame.\n\nAlso curtains: current left curtain covers part of window frame and extends to 632. They are bland. We can add visible folds more strongly and maybe sheer inner layer? Right now the tieback isn't evident because curtains hang nearly straight. Shape does narrow at 350 but subtle. It looks like draped columns, acceptable. Need add shadow / pattern. But adding window color will frame nicely. Maybe reduce curtain width or lighten inner edges. Let's see next render.\n\nBackground scene: once visible, may be too bright/desaturated due to glass overlay and warm grade. We'll inspect.\n\nAlso initial window scene drawing order bug: `pg` for hill passes `ImageDraw.Draw(base)` each time okay. Need clipping? scene elements might spill outside pane, but frame overlay will cover boundaries except building. We kept within.\n\nNeed maybe brighten outside with stronger blue and green. Current sky colors will show.\n\nFix frame. Also right backguard clock reposition. Also maybe sink basin issue: opening ellipse at 568-836 with basin gradient polygon over; resulting visual giant white basin as in image. It looks like a modern sink but apron white. Could add edge shading and make opening darker. Let's refine after window.\n\nNeed improve window light / shadow. We can add a warm glow around window after frame, to spill. Already glow. Maybe add visible diagonal sunlight beams once outside visible, but currently barely visible. We'll refine.\n\nLet's patch."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_Ob5mygtwRrfGOLurFiAT6945","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('draw_kitchen.py')\ns=p.read_text()\n# add grad_ring helper after grad_poly\nneedle='''def soft_shape(im, draw_fn, color, blur=10, offset=(0, 0)):'''\nhelper='''def grad_ring(im, b_out, b_in, r_out, r_in, c1, c2, horizontal=False, stops=None):\n    \"\"\"Gradient ring between an outer and an inner rounded rectangle.\"\"\"\n    x0, y0, x1, y1 = bx(b_out)\n    x0 = max(0, x0); y0 = max(0, y0); x1 = min(CW, x1); y1 = min(CH, y1)\n    if x1 <= x0 or y1 <= y0:\n        return\n    g = gradient_size(x1 - x0, y1 - y0, c1, c2, horizontal, stops)\n    mask = Image.new(\"L\", (x1 - x0, y1 - y0), 0)\n    md = ImageDraw.Draw(mask)\n    md.rounded_rectangle((0, 0, x1 - x0 - 1, y1 - y0 - 1), radius=int(r_out * S), fill=255)\n    ix0, iy0, ix1, iy1 = bx(b_in)\n    md.rounded_rectangle((ix0 - x0, iy0 - y0, ix1 - x0, iy1 - y0),\n                         radius=int(r_in * S), fill=0)\n    g.putalpha(mask)\n    im.alpha_composite(g, (x0, y0))\n\n\ndef soft_shape(im, draw_fn, color, blur=10, offset=(0, 0)):'''\ns=s.replace(needle, helper)\nold='''# outer casing\ngrad_rect(base, (218, 72, 1074, 660), \"#d8b98f\", \"#b58a61\", radius=13)\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (226, 80, 1066, 652), 10, None, \"#8f6645\", 2)\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (232, 86, 1060, 646), 8, \"#efdfc1\", \"#f8edda\", 4)\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (242, 96, 1050, 636), 6, \"#d6bd99\", \"#9e7554\", 2)\n# pane frame\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (252, 104, 1040, 628), 4, \"#e9d8b9\")\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (258, 110, 1034, 622), 2, None, \"#a47b58\", 2)'''\nnew='''# outer casing -- ring, so the morning view stays visible\ngrad_ring(base, (218, 72, 1074, 660), (246, 100, 1046, 632), 13, 7,\n          \"#dec29b\", \"#b68a61\", stops=[(0, C(\"#e4caa5\")), (.55, C(\"#cfae86\")),\n                                       (1, C(\"#ae825a\"))])\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (226, 80, 1066, 652), 10, None, \"#8f6645\", 2)\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (232, 86, 1060, 646), 8, None, \"#f8edda\", 2)\n# pane frame ring\ngrad_ring(base, (240, 94, 1052, 638), (258, 110, 1034, 622), 7, 2,\n          \"#f5e8cf\", \"#ddc6a4\", stops=[(0, C(\"#fbf0d9\")), (.6, C(\"#ecdcbe\")),\n                                       (1, C(\"#d3b993\"))])\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (242, 96, 1050, 636), 6, None, \"#9e7554\", 2)\nrr(ImageDraw.Draw(base), (252, 104, 1040, 628), 4, None, \"#a47b58\", 2)'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\n# reposition clock to right of kettle\ns=s.replace('(1288, 620, 1354, 686)', '(1398, 618, 1458, 678)')\ns=s.replace('(1295, 627, 1347, 679)', '(1404, 624, 1452, 672)')\ns=s.replace('''for ang in range(0, 360, 30):\n    x = 1321 + math.cos(math.radians(ang)) * 20\n    y = 653 + math.sin(math.radians(ang)) * 20\n    ln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1321 + math.cos(math.radians(ang)) * 16,\n                              653 + math.sin(math.radians(ang)) * 16), (x, y)], \"#8d7657\", 1)\nln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1321, 653), (1321, 638)], \"#6a533a\", 2)\nln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1321, 653), (1332, 660)], \"#6a533a\", 2)''','''for ang in range(0, 360, 30):\n    x = 1428 + math.cos(math.radians(ang)) * 17\n    y = 648 + math.sin(math.radians(ang)) * 17\n    ln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1428 + math.cos(math.radians(ang)) * 13,\n                              648 + math.sin(math.radians(ang)) * 13), (x, y)], \"#8d7657\", 1)\nln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1428, 648), (1428, 635)], \"#6a533a\", 2)\nln(ImageDraw.Draw(base), [(1428, 648), (1438, 654)], \"#6a533a\", 2)''')\n# nameplate shift left/center remains okay but move to gap below? currently center 1228-1414, may overlap kettle; make small at right lower? leave\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 draw_kitchen.py","description":"Fix window frame ring to reveal view","timeoutMs":180000}}
