l elements overlap. We can build outside scene separately and paste, but easier apply color/saturation adjustment to region just before frame. At that point, window region only view (no frame). Crop and enhance color 1.35, contrast 1.08, brightness 1.02, then paste. That'll make landscape pop. Add stronger sun and light rays.\n\nHowever pasting crop region exactly x251-1038, y109-630 avoids frame.\n```\nfrom PIL import ImageEnhance\ncrop = base.crop(bx((251,109,1038,630)))\ncrop = ImageEnhance.Color(crop).enhance(1.45)\ncrop = ImageEnhance.Contrast(crop).enhance(1.06)\nbase.paste(crop,...)\n```\nNeed do before frame, after glass.\n\nThen add sun glow maybe at correct stage. We can reorder: enhance then draw sun + glow + rays? But sun already part; we can adjust.\n\nWindow scene composition: hills dominate huge midground; horizon at 435, so sky only 45% of window height? Fine. But trees small, one lollipop tree; improve with more layering and foliage. The large trees at x945 etc appear cut and dark. Add a lush garden just outside: closer bushes along bottom, tree canopy top right, fence, maybe distant cottage/chimney? A cozy morning view with a garden and maybe birdhouse. Could add a little greenhouse/cottage? Too much maybe.\n- Add tree crown at top right visible through pane with leaves, framing.\n- Add warm light on hills.\n- Add path and wildflowers more visible.\n- Maybe add a clothesline? no.\n\nOverall composition next issues:\n1. Curtains: still broad flat cream borders with some folds too subtle; but acceptable. They take up much window side. Could add a warm golden lit edge and more shadow folds. The tiebacks read as sticks crossing the window, odd: the horizontal line across the entire window at y=354 is from curtain tieback? Wait there is a long cream diagonal/horizontal bar across both curtains and window at y=350. I see a horizontal white bar spanning from left curtain to right curtain at y~330. That's likely from `soft_poly_shadow`? No. What is it? Looking at image, there's a horizontal pale bar from x250 to 950 at y~330, matching horizontal muntin? Actually window horizontal muntin at y=352-374 extends x=258-1034. It's cream, and appears as a thick horizontal bar across all panes. That's correct muntin. But it visually looks like a rod behind curtains, not a muntin because it extends to curtains? At x=258..1034 yes, and curtains overlap; but window frame muntin should be visible acrosswindow. It's very pale and thick. Fine. Tiebacks at y350 blend with muntin; the tieback cords at x296 and 996 look like knobs. The long bar across is the muntin, okay.\n2. The frame and curtains are beige; could make frame white and curtains with subtle pattern, adding contrast.\n3. Sink: giant white rectangular basin reads more like a studio sink; the white apron is nice but interior is flat grey-white. Add shading and reflections to give depth. Maybe fill basin with warm reflected light and dark interior walls, add a few water drops. The basin opening should read as hole: upper part shadowed, front inner wall lighter, back wall dark, bottom rim. Right now the opening is a large white/grey rectangle due to gradient polygon bright bottom and giant white frame. Could darken interior significantly and reduce size. Also faucet is in front but lip? Sink body at 548-856, basin at 568-836, almost same width, so thin rim. It's farmhouse style; okay. Need make tap connected behind. The water drop is floating.\n4. Cabinets too muted, almost blue-grey. Warm sage green would be cozier. Right side is in shadow and dark. Add stronger warm sunlight raking across doors, maybe make cabinets warmer sage (#6f8268) not gray. Current gradient #7b917c to #425747; output appears gray due to grade/vignette. Increase saturation / warm.\n5. Stove blank cream side. Add decorative details and warmer colors. Clock now visible.\n6. Range backguard very tall and blank; could reduce height to 640? It adds block. Maybe add shelf/rail and copper utensils. Or make it tiled behind. Actually the backguard is a cream panel at x1142-1500 y588-786. It's big. Could decorate with a subtle embossed border and a nameplate. Add small botanical line etching or enamelware. Keep clean.\n7. Kettle overlaps clock? clock now at right of kettle partially overlaps spout? Kettle body ends 1372, clock at 1398, good. Kettle handle extends 1356; okay.\n8. Cabinet drawers on far right x1038-1100 too narrow but okay.\n9. Left wall apron, hat, art nice but all beige; add richer color (rust stripe apron, green herbs).\n10. Window sill cat is cute but slightly blob. Could improve fur texture with small strokes, tail, ears. Already.\n11. Morning light should be warm gold and directional. Add sunlight patch across left counter and cabinet faces, stronger, and darker shadows elsewhere. Right now even low contrast due to haze and broad ambient. Need increase contrast: deepen corners, add glow near window, color grade with warm highlights and cool shadows.\n12. Add steam from mug more visible; currently faint. Could make it soft white, more visible.\n13. Add a second mug? Maybe a small bowl and spoon. But composition maybe enough.\n14. Add stool/rug? bottom fully cabinets, no floor. Could add a small woven rug at bottom in front? It would obscure cabinets and add coziness; but bottom edge 1200 cuts. Maybe a wooden stool with a folded blanket at bottom left foreground would add depth and charm. But risk clutter and user asks cozy kitchen. Could add hanging dried flowers, which exist.\n\nNeed likely need make final image feel high quality and warm. We can iterate. Let's improve outside first with saturation and sun.\n\nImplement:\n- Modify sky base colors more saturated: top #7fb2c4, middle #c9d7c4, horizon #f7d08d. Existing gradient set; change.\n- Sun: place at (880, 235) radius 35, color #fff2c0; multiple glows larger. Draw after sky before hills. Current sun is at 887,210 and a pale dot. Add rays from sun outward as long soft polygons across sky, but maybe not necessary.\n- Add a flatter meadow/garden with warm highlights.\n- Use ImageEnhance on window region after glass.\n\nWhere apply saturation: after glass overlay, before frame. Insert:\n```\nfrom PIL import ImageEnhance\ncrop=...\ncrop = ImageEnhance.Color(crop).enhance(1","truncated":true}
