tends beyond but sky overwrites interior. Do this.\n\nSimilarly, maybe `glass` overlay is mild. `glass` polygon alpha 14, fine.\n`soft_poly_shadow` for muntins overlays thin bars but okay.\nThe curtains shadow covers behind frame? fine.\n\nSun looks like a ring because the disk is drawn with #fff colors then perhaps `soft_poly_shadow` dark overlay; after moving shadow, sun should be bright.\nGlows invisible because also covered by shadow.\n\nLet's move shadow.\n\nAlso note window scene still greenish gray after shadow; will fix dramatically. Great.\n\nOther global layers after objects could mute colors: light beams/glow are additive-ish alpha but low; grade alpha 10; vignette. Fine.\n\nNeed add directional shadow of frame on the wall (outside window), not inside. Our moved shadow does that.\n\nLet's patch: remove current shadow call in frame section, insert before `win = ...` section. Make alpha 95, blur 18, offset. A shadow behind window should be drawn on wall. Then sky draw. Good.\n\nAlso need make sun rays and glow visible; they are inside sky and previously shadowed. Fine.\n\nLet's move and inspect."}
