one cracked? no.\nBowl color: warm white with sage stripe. Add a small blue-grey band along rim? use #8a9f8a.\n\nThis will look like eggs.\n\nSink redesign code. Need ensure towel block replaced after.\n\nLet's write replacement from `# apron front` to before `# faucet`. Then towel.\n\nDetailed:\n```\n# apron front sink\nsoft_poly_shadow(base,[(548,808),(858,808),(858,934),(548,934)],color,alpha,blur,offset)\n# apron body\ngrad_rect(base,(548,820,858,925), \"#f6efe1\",\"#d0c0a5\", radius=14)\n# Actually gradient plus shading\n# top rim slab\nrr(base,(546,780,860,842), 18, fill=\"#f2ebdc\") \n# inner basin gradient rounded\n# Use rr with fill then overlay dark gradient shape.\n# simplest: grad_rect(base,(562,790,844,834), \"#6b6657\",\"#b4a78f\", radius=14, stops)\n# rim ring: rr outline width 6\nrr(... 548,781,858,841, 18, None, \"#f7f0e2\", 8)\n...\n# apron front drawn after rim, from y=838 to 922\ngrad_poly shape\n# top shadow under rim\n# fluted lines\n# bottom curved shadow\n# basin inner details (draw before apron front, after rim maybe)\n```\nNeed layering: First apron body, then rim, then basin opening, then apron front? The apron front overlaps lower rim. Real sink front rises to rim, so yes.\n\nLet's set:\n- Apron body outer: `grad_rect((548,808,858,928), radius=16)` looks like white block. Add side shading.\n- Rim: `rr((544,778,862,840), 18, fill=\"#f6efe1\")`. This is a big white slab over top of apron. Then basin hole: `grad_rect((560,790,846,832), radius=14, dark to light)`.\n- Inner bowl: additional side shadows and water reflection.\n- Apron front: `grad_poly([(550,836),(856,836),(856,902),(847,919),(558,919),(550,902)])` with bright white. But this will cover the lower part of basin hole (y832-840), okay.\n- Rim front edge becomes y=836-842 white.\n- Add shadow line above apron front at y=838.\n- Add towel to left front.\n- The counter top y=788-850; the sink rim at y778-840 sits on top of counter, good. The apron body from 840 down.\n- The sink will