{"type":"thinking","text":"Cabinets are quite flat and gray-green. The sink front looks like a giant white bowl/apron; the towel good. There are weird vertical gaps / panels under sink? The cabinet doors behind the sink are visible below the apron? The sink hangs over a door; normal.\n\nThe counter and cabinets could use more warmth. The flat gray-green reads cold, while the rest is warm. Adjust cabinet color to warmer sage/olive, increase saturation: base #778c6e (warm olive green) to #4a604d. Current #7b917c (cool) and #425747. Use #82946d, #5d7357, #40533f. But final image might look yellow-green; warm morning light would shift green toward olive, cozy. Maybe choose deep sage #5c735f with olive tone #6c7f64. The image currently uses cool sage which contrasts warm wood, a classic palette. It's okay. But coziness might benefit from warmer, slightly desaturated olive. Let's try #7f9270 -> #435742 with a touch more yellow. Need ensure not swampy. Could keep cool as accent.\n\nThe cabinet flatness:\n- Add a stronger gradient to panels (currently subtle) and a highlight along left/upper edges.\n- Add shadows at seams between doors. Currently there are dark lines but thin.\n- Add a warm reflected light along the top rail under the counter. Also the counter overhang shadow could be stronger.\n- Add a soft highlight on the right side of each door from window light.\n- Add brass hardware with shadow.\n\nWe can enhance in `cabinet_door`:\n```\n# frame outer\ngrad ...\n# shadow under top rail and left rail inside panel\nsoft_poly_shadow panel ...\n# inside panel gradient (lighter top-left, darker bottom-right)\n# highlight line at inset top and left, shadow at bottom/right\n# panel subtle vignette\n# hardware shadow\n```\nCurrently panel inset has gradient but perhaps because values too close, invisible. Increase contrast: panel top #6f8570 bottom #4c6250; frame #7a907b.\n- Add a blurred dark inner shadow around inset: create overlay rectangle outline blurred; maybe.\n- Add a warm highlight line along the left vertical frame, thin #9eb09a.\n- Add dark seam at door edges.\n- Add a subtle diagonal reflection across the doors near sink: a soft band from window. Could use screen light after objects; but we can draw an overlay gold alpha 15 with soft edges clipped to cabinets. Add one broad diagonal band across cabinets x780-1120 y850-1150. It would add depth.\n- Add bottom gradient darkening.\n\nLet's improve cabinet_door function. Need ensure sink apron and towel cover center. The crop reveals small dark vertical lines under sink where cabinet doors are behind; fine.\n\nAlso the floor edge at bottom is black gradient. It reads as shadow; okay.\n\nCounter wood: fine.\n\nTiebacks and cabinets are next. Let's inspect window crop updated."}
