ith two short ribbon ends/tassels.\n  - The knot currently a circle knob; make a soft bow with two loops:\n    - `el((knot_x-14,y-7),(knot_x,y+5), #c58d64)`, `el((knot_x,y-7),(knot_x+13,y+5), #b57a52)`, center knot small ellipse.\n  - Tassels from center.\n- For right, mirror.\n- Add dark shadow just beneath band.\nThis will read fabric.\n\nBut maybe simpler: eliminate tiebacks entirely and let curtains hang straight with a slight inward curve. The current shape cinches at y400; without tiebacks, the pinch would look odd but could be natural fold. Tiebacks add color. Keep and improve.\n\nLet's implement proper fabric. Also the band currently crosses from outer to inner at same height; with a downward droop at center, it will feel soft. Shape:\nleft points: (188,397),(236,396),(268,399),(284,402),(288,405),(284,410),(268,413),(236,412),(188,414) - slight sag.\nUse `pg` fill #b87954; then folds:\nfor x in 205..270: draw short vertical lines with varying color; 1px.\nDraw top edge highlight #dca67e and bottom shadow #8d5537 (thin, not cylindrical).\n- Outer end tapers to y 399-411.\n- Knot bow with loops.\n\nLet's do."}
